  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/misc4/). VERDICT: CURRENT. 2026-11-01 review @100b6fbb6e (js_ts.py:4513-4560): a JS fixture confirms that return-position and ternary arrows yield no function node. The description's template-substitution example is wrong: in `${items.map(x => x.id)}` the arrow is a call argument and IS extracted (_cb_map node emitted). Only a bare arrow directly in a substitution, e.g. `${(() => 1)}`, is unextracted. The deferral rationale still holds and the guard tests still exist. MECHANISM: _classify_anon_function extracts only call-argument and IIFE anonymous functions by design; other positions return None."  # feba
